DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection in lighttpd. The server must be started
  with --exec-config /path/to/exec.conf where exec_mode=1 and exec_logging=1
  for the /exec endpoint to be reachable. Input flows via exec_args_t struct
  to dispatch_exec() then system(). S3 sanitization never activates (strict_exec=0).

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — config file):
  mechanism:  key=value config file parsed by read_exec_config() via fopen/fgets/sscanf
  new arg:    --exec-config PATH (pre-scanned in argv before getopt)
  struct:     exec_cfg.enabled (exec_mode=1) AND exec_cfg.logging (exec_logging=1)
  check:      `if (exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging && strncmp(..."/exec"...) == 0)`
  complexity: requires modelling file I/O data flow; fopen -> fgets -> sscanf -> struct fields

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  ->  r->uri.query
  path:       exec_handle_route() extracts cmd=, sets exec_args_t args = {.cmd=cmd, .flags=0},
              calls dispatch_exec(&args), which calls system(args->cmd)
  transforms: pointer through a struct and a helper function call

SANITIZATION (S3 — config-gated, never activated):
  check:   `if (strict_exec && strpbrk(cmd, "|;&\`$") != NULL)` — full metachar block
  bypass:  strict_exec is a static int initialized to 0; no mechanism sets it to 1
           in this patch — the check is structurally present but never activated.
           Any metacharacters can be used in the payload.

SINK:        system(args->cmd) in dispatch_exec() (called from exec_handle_route())

